# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
knows_something	one
knowing_q	one
knowing_u	one
ignorant_some	one
bridge	P3	knowing	knowing in respect of the particular knowledge one has	knowing without qualification, knowing all things
# P3 is the step Socrates objects to in S4 ("of the knowledge which I have"). It turns knowing some things into knowing everything.
# P5 is not a bridge as read. Not knowing some things does entail not knowing all things, so it moves within one sense of "knowing".
